 "14": {
  "text": "AI writes your code faster than your team can review it. Every M R is twice as big as last year. And every dev ships one and a half times more of them. So reviewers run out of attention, and may skip the changes that are actually risky. Meta fixed the attention problem by giving every M R a risk score. Low-risk M R are approved automatically, and humans only review high risk changes. The result? Production incidents down 98%, rollback rates down 30%, and wait time down 33%. Engineers ship faster and safer, while also reviewing less. Here's why inspection matters.",
